      "role": "user",
      "content": "wow, okay, that's definitely a lot more intense. i ran it through the tool again and the score jumped up significantly, so we're definitely in the ballpark now. \n\nbut honestly... reading it out loud, it's getting a little hard to follow. it's starting to sound a bit \"purple\"—lots of big, heavy words everywhere. i know we need the score, but if it's too thick with adjectives, the candidate is going to trip over the words during the speech. \n\ncan you do one more pass? try to find a middle ground where the score stays high—maybe even a bit higher than this one just to be safe for the office—but try to make the flow smoother? i don't want it to feel like a list of descriptors, but we really can't afford a low score from the automated checker. can you balance that out?",
